  "id": "COMPOUND:21112 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Guvacine Hydrochloride appears to have a shared relationship with LAMA-84 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to ZR-75-1, which is targeted by Miltirone and Quercitrin-7-olate, both of which ultimately target LAMA-84. Similarly, Guvacine Hydrochloride is connected to VMRC-LCP, which is targeted by Cocosamide B, also leading to LAMA-84. These pathways suggest a potential mechanism where Guvacine Hydrochloride may influence biological processes through intermediaries that ultimately affect LAMA-84. The evidence points to a possible role of Guvacine Hydrochloride in modulating pathways that are targeted by other compounds, potentially through a common downstream effect on LAMA-84. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible functional link between Guvacine Hydrochloride and LAMA-84, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
